      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In a natural \"model\" of a chronic psychoemotional stress in humans, (neurasthenia) a decrease in the nociceptive threshold was found. The decrease resulting from weakening of supraspinal tonic descending inhibition which, in its turn, evidently was due to a diminished activity (or dysfunction) of the brain opioid system occurring in a long-lasting psychoemotional stress."},
